# AI Hub — the i3 side. Copy the bits you want into ~/.config/i3/config.
#
# The idea: workspace 4 is the AI workspace. The hub lives there, and so does
# any chatbot you open from it.

# 1. Open the hub. bin/ai-hub starts its own local server if needed, then opens
#    the page as an --app window (no tab strip, no address bar).
bindsym $mod+Shift+a exec --no-startup-id ~/i3-setup/ai-hub/bin/ai-hub

# 2. Put the hub on the AI workspace.
#
#    Match on INSTANCE, not class. A Chromium-family browser in --app mode
#    reports the SAME WM_CLASS as every other window of that browser
#    ("Brave-origin" here) and derives the instance from the URL's host, so the
#    hub window is:
#        WM_CLASS(STRING) = "127.0.0.1", "Brave-origin"
#    Check yours with:  xprop WM_CLASS   then click the hub window.
assign [instance="^127\.0\.0\.1$"] → number 4

# 3. Optional: open the hub at login. Use `exec`, not `exec_always`, or an i3
#    restart opens a second copy.
# exec --no-startup-id ~/i3-setup/ai-hub/bin/ai-hub

# 4. Optional: if you also open chatbots as --app windows, they get an instance
#    derived from their own URL, so they can be assigned to the same workspace.
# assign [instance="^(claude\.ai|chatgpt\.com|chat\.deepseek\.com)"] → number 4
